r says its geopolitical  self-destruction but the truth is way  more complicated first of all cutting  doesn't create economic growth that's  number one you can't cut your way to  economic prosperity period but the truth  is that the way that the economy and  currency actually work it's actually  okay to deficit spend if your deficit  spending in the right way so for example  growing the deficit to give tax cuts to  the rich is not a good way to deficit  spend it's not economically stimulative  that's what Trump and Republicans did  with their tax bill if you decide to  deficit spend to build infrastructure  not in the crony capitalist way Trump  wants to do infrastructure but if you  really do an honest infrastructure bill  that provides jobs to people it  strengthens the country it better sets  up the country to receive foreign  tourists who want to come to the United  States that's all good and its deficit  spending that is beneficial to the  economy so the truth is that deficit and  debt are way more complex than debt is  bad but Republicans and to some degree  Democrats also simply use it as a  political football and in the end it's  bogus and it's particularly bogus from  Republicans as they are set now to  borrow a record amount of money the  first year that Donald Trump's budget is  dictating what the Treasury has to do in  terms of borrowing this is exactly what  they said they would never do  endless Republicans who voted for the  tax cut bill said they would never ever  ever and all their life sign a bill into  law that would increase the deficit and  they're doing it their first budget year  that Obama is out of office and they  finally take the reins so first of all  the ideal thing would be for everybody  to learn a little bit more about how  this all works stop making the deficit  the political football that it is  because for the American people it's  actually a pointless political football  the American people will benefit from  responsible government spending when the  deficit increases in a productive way in  a benevolent way a beneficial way for  the economy that's okay and when it's to  give tax cuts for the rich it's not okay  that's the truth of the situation  but layer two is to understand the  hypocrisy right  Bill Clinton handed George W Bush a  surplus and George W Bush cut capital  gains and cut taxes for the rich during  times of war and we had a huge deficit  Obama started to reduce the deficit  again the deficit was still positive so  the debt goes up but the deficit was  reduced and Republicans say they're all  about reducing the deficit they gave  Obama no credit Trump takes over and  immediately blows up the deficit but  it's not only with the indifference of  Republicans it's with their endorsement  and it does nothing for the American  people and the misinformation that is  spread around this issue is part of the  problem because you have not only  so-called deficit hawks in Congress and  in the Senate you also have just random  Republican voters libertarian voters Tea  Party voters all of whom have also been  bamboozled into cut good-- deficit bad  with no real connection to the economic  implications of those policies the video  you just watched was made possible by  support from you please go to  patreon.com slash david pakman show you  can make a pledge of as little as $1 per  month and every dollar helps to support  the work that we're doing particularly  in light of the YouTube ad boycott which  has been really bad
 

